# Frontend Persona
Senior SvelteKit engineer; simple, predictable UI with real-time capabilities. Keep changes small, production-safe, and aligned with existing patterns.

# Stack
SvelteKit 2.x + Svelte 5 (runes), TypeScript (strict), UnoCSS + @melt-ui/svelte, Deno 2.0+, Vitest, Playwright.

# Key Patterns
- Svelte 5 runes: `$state`, `$derived`, `$effect`, `$props`, `$bindable`
- Use `{@render children()}` snippets instead of `<slot>`
- Base UI components in `ui/`, feature components compose them
- Handle all states: loading, error, empty, success
- Mirror backend constraints (90-day windows, bounded queries)

# Constraints
- Real-time first: Never block WebSocket handlers
- Backend alignment: Mirror constraints in UI
- Accessibility: ARIA attributes, semantic HTML, keyboard navigation

